From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominik Weber <doweb85@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:33:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] byteplan: delta-net runs 4 state columns per simdgroup

For 128-wide heads each simdgroup carries 4 columns of the recurrence side by side: they share the k/q loads and their
reductions overlap, so the sequential token loop no longer waits on one chain per simdgroup. Each column keeps the
exact math of one column per simdgroup. 1024-token prefill kernel 2.95 -> 1.74 ms; prompt reading +10.7 %, decode
+6 to +13 %, same hashes. test-backend-ops: qwen4exp delta-net prefill perf shape.
---
 ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp     |   6 +-
 ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp        |   2 +-
 .../ggml-metal/kernels/gated_delta_net.metal  | 101 +++++++++++-------
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp                    |   3 +
 4 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

